 "source": {
  "text": "//@version=6\nindicator(\"UCTPROBE_RS_SYMINFO_INDUSTRY\", overlay = true)\n\n// RS RATING TRANSFER, L3 -- THE CAPTURE THAT WITNESSES `syminfo.industry` / `syminfo.sector`.\n//\n// TradingView's industry and sector strings are its own taxonomy, not UCT's. The engine serves\n// a TradingView string only where a capture witnesses it for that symbol class, the\n// `symbolScope.json` discipline. Capture across many symbols, including ETFs: RS Rating\n// compares `syminfo.industry == 'Investment Trusts/Mutual Funds'`. A TEXT capture: read the\n// last-bar label's text (`objects.texts`), plus the plots below.\n\nif barstate.islast\n    label.new(bar_index, close, \"IND=\" + syminfo.industry + \"|SEC=\" + syminfo.sector + \"|TYPE=\" + syminfo.type)\nplot(str.length(syminfo.industry), \"I01_len_industry\")\nplot(str.length(syminfo.sector), \"I02_len_sector\")\nplot(syminfo.industry == \"Investment Trusts/Mutual Funds\" ? 1 : 0, \"I03_is_fund_industry\")\n// NON-VACUITY CONTROL\nplot(str.length(syminfo.ticker), \"I04_len_ticker_CONTROL\")\n",
  "sha256": "76539c135b16008f845873c52d2155ceeea3070c9eede4195621ff5d71895aae",
